// XFAIL: RT-434: an off `debug_assert` is type-checked but not effect-checked: `debug_assert(say() == 1)`, say printing, in an `#[effects()]` fn builds without --debug-contracts and is refused with it ("'f' is #[effects()], but it does io") (0.30.2)
// From the paused g302debug work (its rt_XXX, from the RT-199 design's
// item 7: the assertion is dropped in contracts/desugar.vl before the
// effects run). Since v0.30.1 at least (the same on v0.30.1). RT-199's
// family (an off `debug` clause never checked); here `debug_assert`.
// The borrow-check form is rt_434b. rustc has no effects; it type- and
// borrow-checks an off `debug_assert!` as it does an on one.
// ERROR: 'f' is #[effects()], but it does io
fn say() -> i64 {
    println("io");
    1
}

#[effects()]
fn f(n: i64) -> i64 {
    debug_assert(say() == 1);
    n
}

fn main() {
    println("{}", f(2));
}
